{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03626",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.53,
      "end_seconds": 6.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "doctor, I've brought them through the observations are done, whenever you need them"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.36,
      "end_seconds": 11.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "So, thank you. Right, hello, what's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.62,
      "end_seconds": 17.67,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.88,
      "end_seconds": 22.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "good, that'll be useful pull up a a chair"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 26.69,
      "end_seconds": 33.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "It's no symptoms, doctor. She didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 33.82,
      "end_seconds": 40.69,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 69, temperature 36.7. Saturation 97 percent, pressure 128 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.27,
      "end_seconds": 44.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "Right, good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.1,
      "end_seconds": 58.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.94,
      "end_seconds": 64.98,
      "duration_seconds": 6.04,
      "text": "Three days, I think... sorry, ten days, I got that wrong."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.93,
      "end_seconds": 71.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.11,
      "text": "Rate it for me, mild, moderate or severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.03,
      "end_seconds": 75.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Erm, about a six out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.63,
      "end_seconds": 79.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.1,
      "end_seconds": 89.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.96,
      "text": "A low blood count on a routine test goes along with it, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 89.58,
      "end_seconds": 96.6,
      "duration_seconds": 7.02,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 96.7,
      "end_seconds": 101.99,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.85,
      "end_seconds": 107.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Uh, I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.21,
      "end_seconds": 117.06,
      "duration_seconds": 7.85,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any heavy periods, blood in the stool, black stools or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.49,
      "end_seconds": 132.76,
      "duration_seconds": 14.27,
      "text": "No, no heavy periods, no blood in the stool, no black stools. I did have slightly tired at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.59,
      "end_seconds": 135.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Is your digestion otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.96,
      "end_seconds": 138.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.52,
      "end_seconds": 142.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "a few questions about your lifestyle now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.1,
      "end_seconds": 155.76,
      "duration_seconds": 9.66,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life. I only drink at family occasions. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.09,
      "end_seconds": 159.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Have you been to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.35,
      "end_seconds": 167.77,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "I, I had my appendix taken out when I was in my twenties."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.28,
      "end_seconds": 170.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Let's run through your medicines."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.21,
      "end_seconds": 181.69,
      "duration_seconds": 9.48,
      "text": "well, you know, it's a... um, I can't remember what it's called it's a small white one"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 183.28,
      "end_seconds": 185.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.84,
      "end_seconds": 200.44,
      "duration_seconds": 13.6,
      "text": "for my cholesterol, I believe my daughter sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Ibuprofen i take it 400 milligrams, most days"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.56,
      "end_seconds": 206.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.64,
      "text": "has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.95,
      "end_seconds": 221.77,
      "duration_seconds": 14.82,
      "text": "Hmm, uh, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.63,
      "end_seconds": 227.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Is there anything relevant on the family side?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.97,
      "end_seconds": 229.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "my son has asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.97,
      "end_seconds": 232.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "What about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.64,
      "end_seconds": 238.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "I've got high cholesterol. I've got depression."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.68,
      "end_seconds": 248.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "From what you've told me, it fits best with iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found. Another possibility is a stomach ulcer from tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.92,
      "end_seconds": 252.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.58,
      "end_seconds": 263.45,
      "duration_seconds": 9.87,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like iron-deficiency anaemia needing a source found, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.44,
      "end_seconds": 278.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "I'm going to order a camera test of the stomach and bowel, for iron-deficiency anaemia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 279.69,
      "end_seconds": 282.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "The earliest is Thursday, 9 am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.32,
      "end_seconds": 298.13,
      "duration_seconds": 14.81,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an iron study for anaemia. I'd rather check than guess, and and this is the quickest way to know more. A coeliac blood test is what I'd like next, for anaemia."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.81,
      "end_seconds": 299.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Right, understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.24,
      "end_seconds": 311.11,
      "duration_seconds": 6.87,
      "text": "You'll be taking ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, three months. It's for iron deficiency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.61,
      "end_seconds": 316.36,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Is that safe with my other medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.95,
      "end_seconds": 336.75,
      "duration_seconds": 19.8,
      "text": "Stop the ibuprofen and we will refer you for scopes. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Come back or go to emergency straight away if the symptoms get worse. Come back after the tests."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 337.85,
      "end_seconds": 340.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "I can manage that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.68,
      "end_seconds": 352.39,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 353.29,
      "end_seconds": 364.55,
      "duration_seconds": 11.26,
      "text": "So, I take the ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day and come back after the tests. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.32,
      "end_seconds": 369.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "yes, exactly right. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.09,
      "end_seconds": 375.39,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "great, you know, thank you for your help"
    }
  ]
}